From 02a79dfc24f20f63edcc403d2919bed220a268da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:53:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: retain host working directory for hooks in remote
 sessions

Remote environment selection replaces the turn's executor working directory.
Keep the session host cwd separately so host command hooks can still spawn,
while selected local environments retain priority and remote tool paths stay
unchanged. Use the same host fallback for tool and lifecycle hook requests.

Add a regression that runs a host PostToolUse command with a remote-only
selection and checks its blocking feedback, local selection priority, and
preserved remote tool cwd. The unchanged source fails with ENOENT; the
candidate passes all eight hook runtime tests through the maintained runner.
